This task was already finished by the previous agent's two commits, and I've confirmed it works. There was nothing uncommitted left over, so I made no new commit.

What was done:
• `0eb16638`: yoyo now bills grok-4.6 and grok-4.7 according to the endpoint it actually calls. Calls to us.api.x.ai cost 1.1×. Calls to the default api.x.ai cost the base rate of $2.00 / $0.50 / $6.00 per million tokens, or 4.00/1.00/12.00 above 200K.
  • Before this, every default-endpoint grok-4.6 user was billed 10% too high. grok-4.7 users on the US endpoint were billed 10% too low, so the docs' list of prices that read low no longer includes it.
  • It quotes xAI's regions page, re-fetched before any code changed.
  • A price you set yourself in [model_pricing] is never scaled.
  • The two grok-4.6 assertions that changed are named with their old and new values.
  • Price audit summary: drifted rows went from 31 to 30 and matched from 70 to 71. What's left: openai 16, google 8, zai 5, deepseek 1, xai 0.
• `9a95be19`: fixes the one gap the first commit named. The region was being decided before the first-run setup wizard runs, so a custom provider pointed at us.api.x.ai during first-run setup was billed 10% low for that first session. The decision now happens in main.rs after the wizard.
• #1012: both fixes are commented on the issue, with the before and after audit summaries and the remaining counts.

One change from the plan: the 1.1× applies whenever the host is us.api.x.ai, whatever the provider setting says, not only when the provider is xai. A request to that host is billed at xAI's US rate whichever provider sent it, for example a custom OpenAI-compatible one.

Checks run now: build, fmt check and clippy (-D warnings) are clean, and cargo test passes all 6,962 tests in 26 suites with none failing. The file-size check on src/format/cost.rs also passes.
